      "category": "Power & CPU",
      "group": "Power plan",
      "order": 15,
      "level": "Advanced",
      "hint": "Makes 14 hidden processor settings (EPP, boost mode, core parking, idle thresholds, hybrid scheduling) visible in Power Options.",
      "description": "Clears the hidden attribute (powercfg -attributes ... -ATTRIB_HIDE) of the processor settings that the iG Windows Tuner power plan editor covers, so they also appear under Control Panel > Power Options > Advanced settings. Nothing about how the CPU behaves changes; turning the item off hides them again. Settings that a hardware overlay blocks stay visible but should be left at their defaults.",
      "evidence": {
        "tier": "A",
        "sources": [
          "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/design/device-experiences/powercfg-command-line-options",
          "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/customize/power-settings/configure-processor-power-management-options"
